# Line endings
#
# Everything in the repository is stored with LF. Windows checkouts still get
# LF in the working tree, which is what Node, ESLint, Prisma and the test runner
# all expect — the CRLF files this repo used to contain broke scripted edits
# that matched on "\n}\n\n".
#
# NOTE: history before 2026-08-24 stored CRLF. Normalising it is a deliberate,
# separate commit: `git add --renormalize .` then commit on its own, so the
# whole-file diff does not hide a real change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell is happier with CRLF, and these two are run by hand on Windows.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.psm1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Prisma stores a SHA-256 of each migration.sql in `_prisma_migrations` and
# refuses to continue if the file no longer hashes to the recorded value. CRLF in
# the working tree would change that hash, so these stay LF on every machine even
# if the blanket rule above is ever relaxed.
prisma/migrations/**/*.sql text eol=lf

# Never touch these — normalisation corrupts them.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary

# Generated: collapse in diffs and reviews, they are not hand-edited.
package-lock.json -diff linguist-generated
